IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oas-core-periods`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-payment`
IMPORT `oa2-part3-payment`

-- Tests of oa2-part3-payment: sections 23 to 26. Every expected value is worked out by hand from the words of the
-- section, with the reasoning in the comment.

§ `Section 23 -- commencement`

-- (1): approved on March 10, 2024: payment commences in the first month after: April 2024. Approved on December 20:
-- January of the next year.
#ASSERT `s 23(1): the first month for which payment of the allowance commences` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 10) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1)
#ASSERT `s 23(1): the first month for which payment of the allowance commences` (YearMonthDay 2024 12 20) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1)
-- (1): received March 5, approved April 10 (after the last day of March): the approval may be effective as of a prescribed
-- earlier date not before March 5: March 5 itself and March 20 are accepted; March 4 is not.
#ASSERT `s 23(1): the earlier date as of which the approval may be effective` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2024 4 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 3 5)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 3 5)
#ASSERT `s 23(1): the earlier date as of which the approval may be effective` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2024 4 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 3 20)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 3 20)
#ASSERT `s 23(1): the earlier date as of which the approval may be effective` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2024 4 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 3 4)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Approved on March 31, the last day of the month of receipt: not "after the last day of the month": nothing. No date
-- prescribed: nothing.
#ASSERT `s 23(1): the earlier date as of which the approval may be effective` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2024 3 31) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 3 20)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(1): the earlier date as of which the approval may be effective` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 3 20)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 3 20)
#ASSERT `s 23(1): the earlier date as of which the approval may be effective` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2024 4 10) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1.1): the requirement waived in September 2022: payment may not commence before October 2021 (eleven months earlier).
#ASSERT `s 23(1.1): the earliest month in which payment of the allowance may commence` (YearMonthDay 2022 9 15) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2021 10 1)
-- (2): born March 15, 1960, attained 60 on March 15, 2020. Application received September 10, 2022: one year before is
-- September 10, 2021, which is later than the 60th birthday: the earliest day is September 10, 2021.
#ASSERT `s 23(2): the earliest day to which the approval may be made effective` (YearMonthDay 1960 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2022 9 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 9 10)
-- Received April 1, 2020, just after the 60th birthday: one year before is April 1, 2019, earlier than the birthday: the
-- earliest day is March 15, 2020.
#ASSERT `s 23(2): the earliest day to which the approval may be made effective` (YearMonthDay 1960 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15)
-- Received before the 60th birthday, or on it: "attained the age of sixty years before the day on which the application was
-- received" is not met: nothing.
#ASSERT `s 23(2): the earliest day to which the approval may be made effective` (YearMonthDay 1960 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(2): the earliest day to which the approval may be made effective` (YearMonthDay 1960 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(2): the earliest day to which the approval may be made effective` (YearMonthDay 1960 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 16) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15)
-- The prescribed day is acceptable if not before the earliest day.
#ASSERT `s 23(2): the approval may be effective as of the day prescribed` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 9 10)) (YearMonthDay 2021 9 10)
#ASSERT `s 23(2): the approval may be effective as of the day prescribed` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 9 10)) (YearMonthDay 2022 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(2): the approval may be effective as of the day prescribed` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 9 10)) (YearMonthDay 2021 9 9)
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(2): the approval may be effective as of the day prescribed` NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2022 1 1)
-- (3): all four conditions needed.
#ASSERT `s 23(3): payment of the allowance commences in respect of the month of release` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(3): payment of the allowance commences in respect of the month of release` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(3): payment of the allowance commences in respect of the month of release` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(3): payment of the allowance commences in respect of the month of release` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(3): payment of the allowance commences in respect of the month of release` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `Sections 24 and 25 -- consideration, notice, payment in arrears`

#ASSERT `s 24(1): the Minister must consider without delay whether the applicant is entitled to be paid an allowance` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 24(1): the Minister must consider without delay whether the applicant is entitled to be paid an allowance` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 24(1): the Minister must consider without delay whether the applicant is entitled to be paid an allowance` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 24(2): the Minister must forthwith notify the applicant in writing of the basis on which the amount was fixed` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 24(2): the Minister must forthwith notify the applicant in writing of the basis on which the amount was fixed` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 24(2): the Minister must forthwith notify the applicant in writing of the decision that no allowance may be paid and the Minister's reasons` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 24(2): the Minister must forthwith notify the applicant in writing of the decision that no allowance may be paid and the Minister's reasons` FALSE
-- Ordinary: March 2024 is paid at the end of March; the first month payable is January 2024, approved on January 20.
#ASSERT (`s 25: the end-of-month days on which payment of the allowance for the month may be made` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 1 20))'s `the earliest day` EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2024 3 31)
#ASSERT (`s 25: the end-of-month days on which payment of the allowance for the month may be made` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 1 20))'s `the latest day` EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2024 3 31)
-- Approved on March 15, after the end of January: February's payment may be made at the end of March or of April.
#ASSERT (`s 25: the end-of-month days on which payment of the allowance for the month may be made` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 10) (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 3 15))'s `the earliest day` EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2024 3 31)
#ASSERT (`s 25: the end-of-month days on which payment of the allowance for the month may be made` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 10) (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 3 15))'s `the latest day` EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2024 4 30)
-- April, after the month of approval: ordinary again.
#ASSERT (`s 25: the end-of-month days on which payment of the allowance for the month may be made` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 10) (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 3 15))'s `the earliest day` EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2024 4 30)
#ASSERT (`s 25: the end-of-month days on which payment of the allowance for the month may be made` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 10) (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 3 15))'s `the latest day` EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2024 4 30)
-- Approved on January 31 (not after the end of January): ordinary.
#ASSERT (`s 25: the end-of-month days on which payment of the allowance for the month may be made` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 1 31))'s `the latest day` EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2024 1 31)

§ `Section 26 -- application of Part II`

#ASSERT `s 26(1): sections 14, 15 and 18 apply by virtue of section 26(1) in respect of the benefit` Allowance
#ASSERT NOT `s 26(1): sections 14, 15 and 18 apply by virtue of section 26(1) in respect of the benefit` Pension
#ASSERT NOT `s 26(1): sections 14, 15 and 18 apply by virtue of section 26(1) in respect of the benefit` Supplement
#ASSERT `s 26(1.1): the Minister may waive the requirements of subsections 14(1) and 15(1) and (2) in respect of an application for an allowance` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 26(1.1): the Minister may waive the requirements of subsections 14(1) and 15(1) and (2) in respect of an application for an allowance` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 26(2): subsection 11(2) and sections 16 to 18 apply in respect of the supplement` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 26(2): subsection 11(2) and sections 16 to 18 apply in respect of the supplement` FALSE
